<title>JAPAN: Nippon Television's shares climb on higher profits.</title>
<headline>Nippon Television's shares climb on higher profits.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Nippon Television Network Corp climbed on Wednesday morning, helped by the broadcasting company's higher interim profits announced on Tuesday, traders said.</p>
<p>As of 0112 GMT, the share price was up 300 yen at 33,000 yen, in a turnover of 6,540 shares.</p>
<p>Nippon Television said its parent current profits jumped to 17.9 billion yen in the six months to September 30, up 38.6 percent from the year-ago period.</p>
